Z||000000||TRL46202||12-16-1999||10:08 AM||||Where can I purchase a new vacum tube?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||12-16-1999||10:08 PM||||Not sure what you mean. Do you mean the skinny plastic tubing that goes all over the top of the engine? Or the assembly that is above the drive belt, with all of the hoses on it, and the electrical connector? Or the metal tube that goes from the EGR valve to the bottom of the intake plenum? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||TRL46202||12-17-1999||11:07 AM||||The skinny plastic tubing that connects to the egr valve...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-17-1999||08:57 PM||||Hmmmm... Anybody else? <BR>If it were me, I would just buy some vacuum hose from the parts store. (If your original tube is just broken, but all still there, you can make a "butt-splice" out of a 1.5"-2" length of hose.) Then I would keep my eyes open for what I really need. Check "recycle yards", etc. And keep asking here, from time to time. <BR>From the 22P book... It looks like the original tube was actually part of a "harness" of sorts. Most all of the plastic tubing was sold as one part # -10040419. GM probably doesn't sell it any more. If they do, it's expensive. Good luck!||||reg||1
